{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979143014,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_PvRKBySn8TudJL5n9y10Iz6j","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"squamous|cuboidal|columnar cuboidal|flattened|PATO:0002254","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology","include":"cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 126 matches (showing first 100)\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 4519: # Class: obo:CL_0000075 (columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell)\n\n  Line 4521: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0002065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000075 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.\")\n\n  Line 4522: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000075 \"columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 4525: # Class: obo:CL_0000076 (squamous epithelial cell)\n\n  Line 4528: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000076 \"squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 4533: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\n\n  Line 4536: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000077 \"Mesothelial cells, which morphologically resemble squamous epithelial cells, express both epithelial markers (cytokeratins) and mesenchymal markers (vimentin), reflecting their mesodermal origin. They feature surface microvilli and apical-basal polarity. Under certain conditions, they can undergo mesothelial-to-mesenchymal transition. These cells also produce extracellular matrix proteins, maintain serosal homeostasis, and facilitate fluid transport.\")\n\n  Line 4656: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D007728\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771589\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17105582\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000091 \"A tissue-resident macrophage of the reticuloendothelial system found on the luminal surface of the hepatic sinusoids involved in erythrocyte clearance. Markers include F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, CD163/SRCR-positive. Irregular, with long processes including lamellipodia extending into the sinusoid lumen, have flattened nucleus with cytoplasm containing characteristic invaginations of the plasma membrane (vermiform bodies); lie within the sinusoid lumen attached to the endothelial surface; derived from the bone marrow, form a major part of the body's mononuclear phagocyte system.\")\n\n  Line 4906: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D042783\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21275341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Endothelial_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://sourceforge.net/tracker/?func=detail&atid=440764&aid=3364936&group_id=36855\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000115 \"An endothelial cell comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures and can be squamous or cuboidal. In mammals, endothelial cell has vimentin filaments and is derived from the mesoderm.\")\n\n  Line 4911: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000115 \"From FMA: 9.07.2001: Endothelial cell has always been classified as a kind of epithelial cell, specifically a squamous cell but that is not true. First, endothelial cell can either be squamous or cuboidal (e.g. high-endothelial cell) and secondly, it has different embryological derivation (mesodermal) than a true epithelial cell (ectodermal and endodermal). The basis for present classification is the fact that it comprises the outermost layer or lining of anatomical structures (location-based) but a better structural basis for the differentia is the cytoskeleton of the cell. Endothelial cell has vimentin filaments while an epithelial cell has keratin filaments. [Onard].\")\n\n  Line 5084: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21976958\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23284695\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34741068\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36769303\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000132 \"An hexagonal, flattened, mitochondria-rich endothelial cell that forms a monolayer on the posterior surface of the cornea (the corneal endothelium). Corneal endothelial cells are derived from the neural crest and are responsible for keeping the cornea transparent by maintaining the tissue in a semi-dry state through the action of their ionic pumps and tight junction barrier.\")\n\n  Line 6088: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000239 \"All brush border cells are columnar-cuboidal.  The formal logical definition of this term asserts this. Brush border epithelial cells are predominantly found lining the small intestine and the proximal tubules of the kidneys.\")\n\n  Line 6093: # Class: obo:CL_0000240 (stratified squamous epithelial cell)\n\n  Line 6095: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_squamous_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000240 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of squamous epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cells. The basal layer is directly attached to the basement membrane and the apical layer consists of flattened squamous cells. This provides a protective barrier, commonly found in areas subject to abrasion, such as the skin, oral cavity, and esophagus.\")\n\n  Line 6096: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000240 \"stratified squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 6100: # Class: obo:CL_0000241 (stratified cuboidal epithelial cell)\n\n  Line 6102: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_cuboidal_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000241 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of cuboidal epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cuboidal cells forming the apical layer. This provides a protective lining for ducts in large glands, such as sweat glands.\")\n\n  Line 6103: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000241 \"stratified cuboidal epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 6129: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000244 \"A cell characteristically found lining hollow organs that are subject to great mechanical change due to contraction and distention; originally thought to represent a transition between stratified squamous and columnar epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 6589: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15749908\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19256306\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19727116\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29713660\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37873034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000312 \"An epithelial cell of stratified squamous tissues, including skin, oral mucosa (Hiroshima et al., 2011), and esophagus (Whelan et al., 2018), that produces keratin proteins and secretes antimicrobial peptides to form a resilient barrier against environmental damage, dehydration, pathogens, and microbial invasion. It undergoes successive stages of differentiation marked by changes in keratin expression, supporting tissue integrity, wound repair, and contributing to immune defense.\")\n\n  Line 7726: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000463 \"While insect epidermis is generally columnar/cuboidal, there are certainly well studied cases where it is not (e.g.- Rhodnius prolixus when starved). So it would be safer to add this as a differentium for particular species where this is known. -DSJ.\")\n\n  Line 9274: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000634 \"A cuboidal cell which along with Boettcher's cells form the floor of the external spiral sulcus, external to the organ of Corti.\")\n\n  Line 9749: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000686 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell that secretes cerebrospinal fluid.\")\n\n  Line 14627: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20054144\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29463737\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002062 \"A squamous pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell that is flattened and branched. A pulmonary alveolar type 1 cell covers more than 98% of the alveolar surface. This large cell has thin (50-100 nm) cytoplasmic extensions to form the air-blood barrier essential for normal gas exchange.\")\n\n  Line 14636: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002062 \"squamous alveolar cell\")\n\n  Line 14637: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002062 \"squamous alveolar lining cell\")\n\n  Line 14651: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0412046911\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36138472\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8540632\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002063 \"A pulmonary alveolar epithelial cell that modulates the fluid surrounding the alveolar epithelium by secreting and recycling surfactants via specialized organelles called alveolar lamellar bodies. This cell type also contributes to tissue repair and can differentiate after injury into a pulmonary alveolar type 1 cell. This cuboidal cell is thicker than squamous alveolar cells, has a rounded apical surface that projects above the level of the surrounding epithelium, and its free surface is covered by short microvilli.\")\n\n  Line 14656: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002063 \"cuboidal type II cell\")\n\n  Line 15664: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:068340007X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002153 \"The dead keratin-filled squamous cell of the stratum corneum. This cell type lacks a nucleus.\")\n\n  Line 15730: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5686391\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002160 \"A cell type found in the basal epithelial layer on the external side of the tympanic membrane. Cell type is flattened with intracellular spaces of variable dimensions.\")\n\n  Line 15746: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:5686391\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002162 \"An extremely flattened cell type found on the inner side of the tympanic membrane. The surface of this cell type carries sparse pleomorphic microvilli that are more common near the junctional zones.\")\n\n  Line 16022: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15840009\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002188 \"An endothelial cell that is part of the glomerulus of the kidney. This cell is flattened, highly fenestrated, and plays a vital role in the formation of glomerular ultrafiltrate.\")\n\n  Line 16035: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:1416031855\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29262154\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30355494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30725734\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32843640\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Stratum_granulosum\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002189 \"A keratinocyte located in the stratum granulosum of the epidermis, characterized by the presence of keratohyalin granules containing filaggrin—which aggregate keratin filament —and by lamellar granules that secrete lipids and enzymes essential for forming the skin’s waterproof barrier. As these cells progress toward the surface, they adopt a flattened morphology and initiate keratinization to become corneocyte and form the protective stratum corneum. In human epidermis, granular keratinocytes are transcriptomically distinguished by high expression of differentiation markers such as DSC1, KRT2, IVL, and TGM3 (Wang et al., 2020), and LOR, FLG, and SPINK5 (Cheng et al., 2018).\")\n\n  Line 16046: # Class: obo:CL_0002190 (squamous cell of epidermis)\n\n  Line 16052: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002190 \"squamous cell of epidermis\")\n\n  Line 16387: # Class: obo:CL_0002221 (keratinized squamous cell of esophagus)\n\n  Line 16389: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11694559\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002221 \"A squamous cell that has keratin in the esophagus.\")\n\n  Line 16393: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002221 \"keratinized squamous cell of esophagus\")\n\n  Line 16411: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002223 \"A cell of the transparent layer of simple cuboidal epithelium over the anterior surface of the lens; transform into lens fiber(s).\")\n\n  Line 16420: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lens_%28anatomy%29#Lens_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002224 \"A cell of the cuboidal epithelium that covers the lens. The cells of the lens epithelium regulate most of the homeostatic functions of the lens. As ions, nutrients, and liquid enter the lens from the aqueous humor, Na+/K+ ATPase pumps in the lens epithelial cells pump ions out of the lens to maintain appropriate lens osmolarity and volume, with equatorially positioned lens epithelium cells contributing most to this current. The activity of the Na+/K+ ATPases keeps water and current flowing through the lens from the poles and exiting through the equatorial regions. The cells of the lens epithelium also serve as the progenitors for new lens fibers. It constantly lays down fibers in the embryo, fetus, infant, and adult, and continues to lay down fibers for lifelong growth.\")\n\n  Line 16633: # Class: obo:CL_0002244 (squamous cell of ectocervix)\n\n  Line 16635: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32644501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/j.autneu.2015.04.008\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.bu.edu/histology/p/19404loa.htm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002244 \"A stratified squamous epithelial cell located in the ectocervix.\")\n\n  Line 16639: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002244 \"ectocervical squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 16640: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002244 \"squamous cell of ectocervix\")\n\n  Line 16788: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31869123\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002258 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the thyroid follicle epithelium, with a shape that ranges from squamous when inactive to cuboidal or columnar when active, reflecting its hormonal activity. Its apical surface is lined with microvilli projecting into the colloid-filled lumen, where it synthesizes, stores, and secretes the thyroid hormones thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), releasing them into the bloodstream in response to thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH).\")\n\n  Line 17479: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14592528\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002318 \"A mesothelial cell capable of circulating in the blood by first losing its squamous character. This cell can incorporate into the regenerating mesothelium.\")\n\n  Line 17689: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15339667\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20568222\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9520465\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002337 \"A stem cell found in the basal layer of the epidermis, hair follicle, and sebaceous gland, characterised by its quiescent nature, high proliferative potential, and capacity for long-term self-renewal. This cell maintains epidermal homeostasis by producing transit-amplifying cells that differentiate to replenish the stratified squamous epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 17950: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:9780702029585\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002363 \"A keratocyte is a specialized fibroblast residing in the cornea stroma that has a flattened, dendritic morphology; located between the lamellae with a large flattened nucleus, and lengthy processes which communicate with neighboring cells. This corneal layer, representing about 85-90% of corneal thickness, is built up from highly regular collagenous lamellae and extracellular matrix components. Keratocytes play the major role in keeping it transparent, healing its wounds, and synthesizing its components. This cell type secretes collagen I, V, VI, and keratan sulfate.\")\n\n  Line 19145: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cjm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0006420\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002481 \"The flattened smooth myoepithelial cells of mesodermal origin that lie just outside the basal lamina of the seminiferous tubule.\")\n\n  Line 19688: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23720296\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002538 \"An epithelial cell of the intrahepatic portion of the bile duct. These cells are flattened or cuboidal in shape, and have a small nuclear-to-cytoplasmic ratio relative to large/extrahepatic cholangiocytes.\")\n\n  Line 20745: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002651 \"An endothelial cell that is part of the venous sinus of spleen. This endothelial cell has an elongated, spindle-shaped, flattened morphology that is parallel to long axis of sinus. This cell type rests on a basement membrane interrupted by numerous narrow slits.\")\n\n  Line 20765: # Class: obo:CL_0002653 (squamous endothelial cell)\n\n  Line 20767: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dos\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002653 \"A squamous shaped endothelial cell.\")\n\n  Line 20770: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002653 \"squamous endothelial cell\")\n\n  Line 20855: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022771\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002662 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the lactiferous duct. This cuboidal epithelial cell expresses keratin-18 and is estrogen-receptor alpha positive.\")\n\n  Line 22441: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005009 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney which regulates sodium and potassium balance. The activity of sodium and potassium channels on the apical membrane of the cell is regulated by aldosterone and vasopressin. In mammals this cell type is located in the renal collecting duct system.\")\n\n  Line 22448: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005010 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney that regulates acid/base balance.\")\n\n  Line 22460: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005011 \"A cuboidal epithelial cell of the kidney which secretes acid and reabsorbs base to regulate acid/base balance.\")\n\n  Line 22470: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28400610\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38032388\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005012 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell with multiple motile cilia on its apical surface. These cells facilitate the movement of liquids such as mucus or cerebrospinal fluid across the epithelial surface.\")\n\n  Line 23131: # Class: obo:CL_0008040 (squamous endothelial cell of venule)\n\n  Line 23133: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0008040 \"An endothelial cell of the venule that is squamous shaped. This is in contrast to the cubodial shape of high endothelial venule cells.\")\n\n  Line 23136: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0008040 \"squamous endothelial cell of venule\"@en)\n\n  Line 23956: # Class: obo:CL_0009066 (stratified squamous epithelial cell of anal canal)\n\n  Line 23958: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3440-1876\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009066 \"A stratified squamous epithelial cell that is part of the anal canal.\")\n\n  Line 23960: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009066 \"anal canal stratified squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 23963: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009066 \"stratified squamous epithelial cell of anal canal\")\n\n  Line 24265: # Class: obo:CL_0009096 (esophagus non-keratinized squamous epithelial cell)\n\n  Line 24267: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11694559\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009096 \"Any cell that is part of the esophageal non-keratinized stratified squamous epithelium. In humans, the esophagus, which requires flexibility to accommodate swallowing of a bolus, is covered with a non-keratinized epithelium.\")\n\n  Line 24271: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"esophageal non-keratinized squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 24272: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"esophageal nonkeratinized squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 24273: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"esophagus non-keratinizing squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 24274: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"esophagus nonkeratinizing squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 24275: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"non-keratinized squamous epithelial cell of esophagus\")\n\n  Line 24276: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"non-keratinizing squamous epithelial cell of esophagus\")\n\n  Line 24277: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"nonkeratinized squamous epithelial cell of esophagus\")\n\n  Line 24278: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009096 \"nonkeratinizing squamous epithelial cell of esophagus\")\n\n  Line 24279: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009096 \"esophagus non-keratinized squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 26120: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FMA:256516\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_1000298 \"squamous mesothelial cell of dura mater\")\n\n  Line 26923: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:3926620\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000398 \"An endothelial cell that is part of the hepatic sinusoid. These cells possess flattened areas containing perforations about 0.1 micrometers in diameter, known as fenestrae. The fenestrae are arranged in groups known as sieve plates.\")\n\n  Line 27601: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16550043\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18356246\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000488 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the bile duct. Cholangiocytes contribute to bile secretion via net release of bicarbonate and water. They are cuboidal epithelium in the small interlobular bile ducts, but become columnar and mucus secreting in larger bile ducts approaching the porta hepatis and the extrahepatic ducts.\")\n\n  Line 28770: # Class: obo:CL_1001575 (uterine cervix squamous cell)\n\n  Line 28774: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1251\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001575 \"cervix squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28775: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1251\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001575 \"cervix squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28776: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1251\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001575 \"cervix, uterine squamous epithelial cells\")\n\n  Line 28777: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1251\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001575 \"uterine cervix squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28778: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1251\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001575 \"uterine cervix squamous epithelial cells\")\n\n  Line 28779: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001575 \"uterine cervix squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28783: # Class: obo:CL_1001576 (oral mucosa squamous cell)\n\n  Line 28787: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1252\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001576 \"oral cavity mucosa squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28788: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1252\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001576 \"oral cavity mucosa squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28789: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1252\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001576 \"oral mucosa squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28790: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1252\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001576 \"oral mucosa squamous epithelial cells\")\n\n  Line 28791: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001576 \"oral mucosa squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28794: # Class: obo:CL_1001577 (tonsil squamous cell)\n\n  Line 28798: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1253\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001577 \"tonsil squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28799: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1253\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001577 \"tonsil squamous epithelial cells\")\n\n  Line 28800: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1253\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001577 \"tonsillar squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28801: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1253\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001577 \"tonsillar squamous epithelial cell\")\n\n  Line 28802: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001577 \"tonsil squamous cell\")\n\n  Line 28806: # Class: obo:CL_1001578 (vagina squamous cell)\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 126 matches (26 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":126,"truncated":true},"title":"squamous|cuboidal|columnar cuboidal|flattened|PATO:0002254","time":{"start":1778979142936,"end":1778979143009}},"id":"prt_e336b7d0d001jBLySuWcWotjv6","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","messageID":"msg_e336b6429001HZx4ApW4onvYHU"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979143035,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_Fm2vROJIjz32S1UdUJinK9t1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"has_characteristic|characteristic","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs","include":"*.md"},"output":"Found 16 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md:\n  Line 211: 'mature basophil' subClassOf ('has part' some (nucleus and ('has characteristic' some lobed)))\n\n  Line 213: ## Recording general cellular characteristics\n\n  Line 217: characteristics of cells, such as their morphology. These are recorded\n\n  Line 218: using [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053).\n\n  Line 221: characteristic (e.g,.’ increased branchiness’). The following list of\n\n  Line 230: subClassOf [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n\n  Line 236: ‘Betz cell’ subClassOf ‘has characteristic’ some ‘standard pyramidal morphology’\n\n  Line 242: characteristic'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053) relation.\n\n  Line 248: [platelet](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000233) subClassOf (['has_characteristic'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053) *some* [**anucleate**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001405))\n\n  Line 251: based on these characteristics.\n\n  Line 255: cell and ('has characteristic' some multinucleate) SubClassOf 'has part'\n\n\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/Create_upper_level_slim.md:\n  Line 26: - Create a CSV table with the following characteristics (Find examples in `src/templates`):\n\n\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/editing_guidelines.md:\n  Line 173: If you are unsure whether a characteristic of a cell should be expressed as a relationship or as a differentium in a logically defined class: use a relationship.\n\n\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/LLM_prompt_guidelines_for_CL_definitions.md:\n  Line 13: > 1. Avoid naming the cell type being defined directly. It should start with a statement of a general classification for the cell type being defined, followed by the characteristics that distinguish it from other cell types within the same general classification.\n\n  Line 14: > 2. Describe distinguishing characteristics, including structural features, functional roles, and anatomical context.\n\n  Line 23: > \"A tuft cell that is part of the medullary epithelium of the thymus, characterized by lateral microvilli and specific markers, including L1CAM (1) in both mice and humans, as well as MHC II in mice (1,2). This cell is pivotal in immune functions such as antigen presentation, central tolerance, and type 2 immunity. It exhibits characteristics of both a medullary thymic epithelial cell (mTEC) and a peripheral tuft cell. Its development is governed by transcription factors such as POU2F3 (3,4).\"\n","metadata":{"matches":16,"truncated":false},"title":"has_characteristic|characteristic","time":{"start":1778979142952,"end":1778979143032}},"id":"prt_e336b7d21001mKMm0j6DzRTEAb","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","messageID":"msg_e336b6429001HZx4ApW4onvYHU"}}
