{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979149597,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_1IaZyt3nDgH6RysNZaX9YUQU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md","offset":205,"limit":70},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/relations_guide.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n205: e.g. 'melanocyte' subClassOf 'has part' some 'melanosome'\n206: \n207: This GO term can be combined with a PATO quality term (e.g. for shape) where necessary, e.g.\n208: \n209: For example:\n210: \n211: 'mature basophil' subClassOf ('has part' some (nucleus and ('has characteristic' some lobed)))\n212: \n213: ## Recording general cellular characteristics\n214: \n215: The ontology [<u>PATO</u>](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/pato),\n216: has a rich set of terms that can be used to record the general\n217: characteristics of cells, such as their morphology. These are recorded\n218: using [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053).\n219: \n220: In choosing PATO terms, avoid those referring to some change in\n221: characteristic (e.g,.’ increased branchiness’). The following list of\n222: examples is not exhaustive:\n223: \n224: ### Recording Morphology\n225: \n226: PATO has a set of general morphology terms which may be applicable to\n227: cells.\n228: \n229: For example, [erythrocyte](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000765)\n230: subClassOf [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053)\n231: *some* [biconcave](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0002039)\n232: \n233: PATO also has a set of terms for [<u>specific cell morphologies</u>](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/pato) (mostly\n234: neuronal), e.g.\n235: \n236: ‘Betz cell’ subClassOf ‘has characteristic’ some ‘standard pyramidal morphology’\n237: \n238: ### Recording nuclear number \n239: \n240: To record the number of nuclei in a cell, use a PATO subclass\n241: under the term ['nucleate quality'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001404) with the ['has\n242: characteristic'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053) relation.\n243: \n244: ![image](https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/assets/112839/4b6aa141-c42f-4bff-9d9e-bdb71a17e882)\n245: \n246: For example, \n247: \n248: [platelet](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000233) subClassOf (['has_characteristic'](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053) *some* [**anucleate**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001405))\n249: \n250: Note - that PATO includes bridging axioms that infer part relationships\n251: based on these characteristics.\n252: \n253: e.g.\n254: \n255: cell and ('has characteristic' some multinucleate) SubClassOf 'has part'\n256: some nucleus\n257:                        \n258: ## Taxon constraints\n259: \n260: See\n261: <https://oboacademy.github.io/obook/explanation/taxon-constraints-explainer/>.\n262: \n\n(End of file - total 262 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"e.g. 'melanocyte' subClassOf 'has part' some 'melanosome'\n\nThis GO term can be combined with a PATO quality term (e.g. for shape) where necessary, e.g.\n\nFor example:\n\n'mature basophil' subClassOf ('has part' some (nucleus and ('has characteristic' some lobed)))\n\n## Recording general cellular characteristics\n\nThe ontology [<u>PATO</u>](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/pato),\nhas a rich set of terms that can be used to record the general\ncharacteristics of cells, such as their morphology. These are recorded\nusing [**'has characteristic'**](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053).\n\nIn choosing PATO terms, avoid those referring to some change in\ncharacteristic (e.g,.’ increased branchiness’). The following list of\nexamples is not exhaustive:\n\n### Recording Morphology","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"docs/relations_guide.md","time":{"start":1778979149561,"end":1778979149593}},"id":"prt_e336b96ec0018Xgli0xj5r6y45","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","messageID":"msg_e336b7de5001lkpJFBIaRkyAhf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979149613,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_vizjVdDrZcOsU34FUIX2yudy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/patterns/cellBearerOfQuality.md","offset":1,"limit":220},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/docs/patterns/cellBearerOfQuality.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # cellBearerOfQuality \n2: \n3: [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/cellBearerOfQuality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/cellBearerOfQuality)\n4: ## Description \n5: \n6: A cell that has a specific quality, such as binucleate.\n7: ## Contributors \n8: * [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432) \n9: * [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165) \n10: ## Name \n11: \n12: {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)} {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)}\n13: \n14: ## Annotations \n15: \n16: * [exact_synonym](http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym): {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)}d {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)}\n17: \n18: ## Definition \n19: \n20: Any {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)} that is {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)}\n21: \n22: ## Equivalent to \n23: \n24: {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)} and ([bearer of](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053) some {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)})\n25: \n26: ## Data preview \n27: | defined_class                             | defined_class_label   | cell                                      | cell_label   | quality                                     | quality_label            |\n28: |:------------------------------------------|:----------------------|:------------------------------------------|:-------------|:--------------------------------------------|:-------------------------|\n29: | [CL:0001061](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0001061) | abnormal cell         | [CL:0000000](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000) | cell         | [PATO:0000460](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000460) | abnormal                 |\n30: | [CL:0000225](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000225) | anucleate cell        | [CL:0000003](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000003) | native cell  | [PATO:0001405](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001405) | anucleate                |\n31: | [CL:0000227](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000227) | binucleate cell       | [CL:0000003](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000003) | native cell  | [PATO:0001406](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0001406) | binucleate               |\n32: | [CL:0000103](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000103) | bipolar neuron        | [CL:0000099](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000099) | interneuron  | [PATO:0070006](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0070006) | bipolar morphology       |\n33: | [CL:4023077](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_4023077) | bitufted neuron       | [CL:0000099](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000099) | interneuron  | [PATO:0070012](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0070012) | bitufted cell morphology |\n34: \n35: See full table [here](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/cellBearerOfQuality.tsv) \n\n(End of file - total 35 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# cellBearerOfQuality \n\n[http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/cellBearerOfQuality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/cellBearerOfQuality)\n## Description \n\nA cell that has a specific quality, such as binucleate.\n## Contributors \n* [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432](https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432) \n* [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6601-2165) \n## Name \n\n{[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)} {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)}\n\n## Annotations \n\n* [exact_synonym](http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym): {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)}d {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)}\n\n## Definition \n\nAny {[cell](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0000000)} that is {[quality](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/PATO_0000001)}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"docs/patterns/cellBearerOfQuality.md","time":{"start":1778979149581,"end":1778979149611}},"id":"prt_e336b97090018cn6axxzJS6745","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","messageID":"msg_e336b7de5001lkpJFBIaRkyAhf"}}
