y.tsv) |\n72: \n73: #### Data preview: \n74: | defined:class                             | defined:class:label                     | anatomical:entity                             | anatomical:entity:label    | cell                                      | cell:label                |\n75: |:------------------------------------------|:----------------------------------------|:----------------------------------------------|:---------------------------|:------------------------------------------|:--------------------------|\n76: | CL:0009032 | B cell of appendix                      | UBERON:0001154 | vermiform appendix         | CL:0000236 | B cell                    |\n77: | CL:0009045 | B cell of medullary sinus of lymph node | UBERON:0009744 | lymph node medullary sinus | CL:0000236 | B cell                    |\n78: | CL:0010007 | His-Purkinje system cell                | UBERON:0004146 | His-Purkinje system        | CL:0000003 | native cell               |\n79: | CL:0002680 | PP cell of intestine                    | UBERON:0000160 | intestine                  | CL:0000696 | PP cell                   |\n80: | CL:0009015 | Peyer's patch follicular dendritic cell | UBERON:0001211 | Peyer's patch              | CL:0000442 | follicular dendritic cell |\n81: \n82: See full table [here](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/cellPartOfAnatomicalEntity.tsv)\n83: ### Taxon specific\n84: *A cell that is restricted to a specific taxon, such as CL:0001200 'lymphocyte of B lineage, CD19-positive' are only in mammals. Note - this is not to be used for any cell that is restricted to a taxon, this is for taxon-specific subclasses of existing cell types. This should hardly ever be used.*\n85: \n86: | Attribute | Info |\n87: |----------|----------|\n88: | IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/taxonSpecific |\n89: | Name | taxonSpecific |\n90: | Classes | CL:0000000, NCBITaxon:1,  |\n91: | Variables | cell (CL:0000000), taxon (NCBITaxon:1)