{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979268513,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d5f8ffeT7HuRxhCKpOV7c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_YTE1rtbCuhIx1rgc7zpN6Ejb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":6090,"limit":30},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n6090: # Class: obo:CL_0000239 (brush border epithelial cell)\n6091: \n6092: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000239 \"An epithelial cell characterized by the presence of a brush border on its apical surface, which increases the surface area for absorption.\")\n6093: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpgi.00005.2011>)\n6094: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 \"PMID:25422372\")\n6095: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000239 \"All brush border cells are columnar-cuboidal.  The formal logical definition of this term asserts this. Brush border epithelial cells are predominantly found lining the small intestine and the proximal tubules of the kidneys.\")\n6096: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000239 \"brush border epithelial cell\")\n6097: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000239 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005903)))\n6098: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000239 obo:CL_0000075)\n6099: \n6100: # Class: obo:CL_0000240 (stratified squamous epithelial cell)\n6101: \n6102: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_squamous_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000240 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of squamous epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cells. The basal layer is directly attached to the basement membrane and the apical layer consists of flattened squamous cells. This provides a protective barrier, commonly found in areas subject to abrasion, such as the skin, oral cavity, and esophagus.\")\n6103: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000240 \"stratified squamous epithelial cell\")\n6104: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000240 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000486) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0002254)))\n6105: \n6106: # Class: obo:CL_0000241 (stratified cuboidal epithelial cell)\n6107: \n6108: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_cuboidal_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000241 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of cuboidal epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cuboidal cells forming the apical layer. This provides a protective lining for ducts in large glands, such as sweat glands.\")\n6109: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000241 \"stratified cuboidal epithelial cell\")\n6110: EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000241 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010077)))\n6111: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000241 obo:CL_0000075)\n6112: \n6113: # Class: obo:CL_0000242 (Merkel cell)\n6114: \n6115: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D018862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19834574\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2274847\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24862916\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30415995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Merkel_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000242 \"A specialized epithelial cell located in the skin epidermis and certain mucosal epithelia. It functions as a mechanoreceptor for light touch by forming synapse-like contacts with somatosensory afferent nerve endings, contributing to slowly adapting type I (SAI) tactile responses. Characterized by dense-core neuroendocrine granules, the Merkel cell exhibits both sensory and neuroendocrine properties, including regulated neurotransmitter release via SNARE complex-dependent mechanisms. Its development in mice depends on the transcription factor Atoh1.\")\n6116: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000242 \"FMA:70548\")\n6117: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000242 \"Merkel's cell\")\n6118: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24862916\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000242 \"MC\")\n6119: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000242 \"Merkel cell\")\n\n(Showing lines 6090-6119 of 35625. Use offset=6120 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Class: obo:CL_0000239 (brush border epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000239 \"An epithelial cell characterized by the presence of a brush border on its apical surface, which increases the surface area for absorption.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpgi.00005.2011>)\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 \"PMID:25422372\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000239 \"All brush border cells are columnar-cuboidal.  The formal logical definition of this term asserts this. Brush border epithelial cells are predominantly found lining the small intestine and the proximal tubules of the kidneys.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000239 \"brush border epithelial cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000239 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005903)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0000239 obo:CL_0000075)\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0000240 (stratified squamous epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_squamous_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000240 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is